cartridge "PARTY IN WILLOW HOLLOW/AMY BIENVENU/2026"

' PARTY IN WILLOW HOLLOW
' An original ColecoVision game in Amy by Amy Bienvenu, 2026.
'
' Pip the fox turns ten, and her woodland friends throw her a party
' under the old willow: an owl, a hedgehog, a raccoon, a bunny and a bear
' cub. Go from game to game across the party map; every game won is a
' present, and every present is a candle on the cake at the end.
'
' Eight minigames:
'   Treasure Hunt (the garden): the raccoon buried the party favours.
'     Dig with the button; the beeps get higher as you get closer.
'   Hide and Seek (the burrow): four friends hide behind the furniture.
'     Listen for giggles, look for the bunny's ears, search with the
'     button.
'   Balloon Pop (the big branch): the owl lets balloons go; throw acorns
'     to pop them, but never the colour the owl hoots (it changes).
'   Musical Chairs (the stump): walk round while the tune plays; when it
'     stops, run to a mushroom stool. One stool fewer every round.
'   Pin the Tail (the parlour): see where the bear's tail goes, then pin
'     it blindfolded, by the hot / cold hints. Three tries.
'   Pass the Parcel (the blanket): when the music stops, grab it first;
'     pressing too early fumbles. Five layers.
'   Sack Race (the meadow): hop only once you have landed; a press in
'     mid-air trips Pip. Beat the bunny, hedgehog and bear.
'   Fireflies at Dusk: catch ten fireflies while they glow.
' The finale: the cake, one candle per present (at least one); blow them out to
' the "Happy Birthday" of the 2006 ColecoVision 10-years cake demo (now
' the 1996-2026 anniversary demo in Amy Studio, by Amy Bienvenu); the
' song itself is in the public domain.
'
' Controls (either joystick): the stick moves Pip; the left button digs,
' searches, throws or blows; the right button too. The keypad is not
' used.
' Everything that matters stays in columns 2-29, inside the TV overscan.
' Pip is sprites 0 and 1, which never flicker; the others take turns when
' more than four share a line. The frame loop is protected from the NMI.

